    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/ai-emerging-literacies-librarian-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "AI & Emerging Literacies Librarian",
      "description": "AI & Emerging Literacies Librarian - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Skip to main content Welcome Home About Virginia Tech Meet Our People Talk To Us Featured Departments Search Jobs My Profile Virginia Tech MENU Campus Photo Tour Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Get to Know Virginia Tech Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Network With Us Student Employment Virginia Tech Human Resources Applicant Login Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search AI & Emerging Literacies Librarian 537678 Blacksburg, Virginia Library Administrative & Professional Dean of Libraries Add to favorites View favorites Job Description The AI & Emerging Literacies Librarian contributes to critical literacy education and student learning in a rapidly evolving digital world. The core duties of this position involve developing a variety of learning opportunities related to artificial intelligence (AI) literacy and other emerging literacies, with a focus on supporting ethical decision-making, responsible use, and critical analysis of societal impact. This position will contribute to student proficiency related to assessing the capabilities of AI tools and experimenting with their use. Building on existing digital literacy initiatives and ongoing work across campus, this position will seek opportunities to contribute to collaborative projects, make connections between programs, and to identify gaps where further literacy programming is needed. The AI & Emerging Literacies Librarian also participates as an active member of the Libraries’ Digital Literacy & Learning Engagement Unit through a variety of team teaching and consultation, participation in collaborative events and projects, and ongoing strategic planning. This position will keep up with trends in the field and continue to look ahead towards needs for other emerging literacies as technology continues to change. Required Qualifications -A terminal degree in a field related to the job duties, such as a Masters in Library and/or Information Science (MLS, MLIS, MIS, etc) from an ALA-accredited graduate program -Experience providing instruction or educational programming to undergraduate students -Evidence of scholarly or professional engagement with ethical issues related to artificial intelligence, including bias, misinformation, intellectual property, environmental impact, and data privacy -Experience developing educational programming related to AI literacy, media literacy, and/or digital literacy -Demonstrated experience with applying current theories, frameworks, and/or best practices for AI literacy in an educational setting -Excellent communication and partnership skills with the ability to engage in cross-functional collaboration Preferred Qualifications -Experience creating instructional videos, infographics, and other digital learning objects -Demonstrated experience with or coursework related to learning theories, critical pedagogy, and/or instructional design -An active research agenda demonstrated through published scholarly work Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular-Continued Appointment Track/Assistant Professor Salary Information $68,000 minimum dependent on qualifications and experience Hours per week 40 hours Review Date 10/14/26 Additional Information The application package needs to include a resume, cover letter addressing the candidate’s experience with the responsibilities associated with the position, and the required and preferred qualifications, and the names of three(3) references and their contact information. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance .  These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Rebecca Osborne at rebeccaao@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) a55320bd Last Name (required) cc68b73a Email (required) 0c692dec Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 76e7ac7f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Library Library Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Dean of Libraries Dean of Libraries First Name (required) 5b6f2345 Last Name (required) 420d005e Email (required) 503965e2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) d3011eb8 Last Name (required) 1f941999 Email (required) 87a33f6d Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Academic Affairs Coordinator Blacksburg Virginia Dean - Architecture Join the College of Architecture, Arts, and Design's undergraduate academic affairs and advising team and contribute to the delivery of a positive student experience. Help us build a better future! Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Computer Science Blacksburg Virginia Computer Science Computer science is changing faster than ever, and today’s questions will shape the field for decades to come. Virginia Tech’s Department of Computer Science is seeking the next generation of faculty to help define what’s next. Apply today! Postdoctoral Associate Alexandria Virginia Housing Research Center Launch the next chapter of your research career with the Virginia Housing Research Center. As a Postdoctoral Associate, you'll work alongside leading researchers to explore housing innovation, inform policy decisions, and create positive impacts for communities throughout Virginia. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Get Directions See All Locations Contact Virginia Tech University Status Principles of Community Privacy Statement Acceptable Use We Remember University Libraries Accessibility Consumer Information Cost & Aid SAFE at VT Policies Equal Opportunity WVTF University Bookstore Jobs at Virginia Tech © 202