    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-financial-compliance-manager-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Financial Compliance Manager",
      "description": "Assistant Financial Compliance Manager - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Skip to main content Welcome Home About Virginia Tech Meet Our People Talk To Us Featured Departments Search Jobs My Profile Virginia Tech MENU Campus Photo Tour Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Get to Know Virginia Tech Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Network With Us Student Employment Virginia Tech Human Resources Applicant Login Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Financial Compliance Manager 537605 Blacksburg, Virginia Sponsored Programs Administrative & Professional Vice President for Research Add to favorites View favorites Job Description Reporting to the Director of Financial Management and Compliance – Post Award, the Assistant Financial Compliance Manager leads the Financial Compliance Team within Virginia Tech’s Office of Sponsored Programs (OSP). This position oversees daily operations, staff development, financial compliance reviews, audit support, data validation, and regulatory reporting for a large and complex sponsored research portfolio in conjunction with the Director for Financial Management and Compliance. Virginia Tech administers more than 3,000 active sponsored research projects with over $460 million of expenditures reported in fiscal year 2026, funded by federal, state, industry, foundation, and international sponsors. The Financial Compliance Team safeguards the university’s research funds by monitoring post-award financial activity and ensuring compliance with applicable federal and state regulations, Uniform Guidance sponsor requirements, university policies and procedures, and the specific terms and conditions of awarded sponsored agreements. Through proactive oversight, the team promotes fiscal stewardship, strengthens internal controls, and mitigates institutional risk. The Assistant Financial Compliance Manager leads, supervises, coaches, mentors, and provides training to the Financial Compliance Team while overseeing key compliance functions by: - Fostering a high-performing and collaborative team culture while ensuring accountability, continuous improvement, and exceptional customer service. - Reviewing expenditures and cost transfers for compliance and allowability. - Coordinating responses to internal and external audits by providing requested information, explanations, and support documentation to the auditors. - Managing the university’s Effort Reporting process. - Providing expert financial compliance guidance to faculty, staff, and OSP colleagues. - Reviewing and updating financial compliance policies and procedures. internal OSP policies and procedures. - Developing and delivering research administration and financial compliance training to university-wide stakeholders. Required Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, business administration, public administration, or related field. • Demonstrated experience in post-award research administration, financial management, grant administration, or financial compliance in a similarly regulated environment. • Financial management experience with sponsored programs (state, federal, university). • Demonstrated knowledge of the OMB Uniform Guidance, Federal Acquisition Regulations, federal cost principles, and sponsor requirements. • Experience reviewing and analyzing financial transactions and identifying compliance risks. • Experience responding to audits, monitoring activities, or compliance reviews. • Strong communication skills for interaction with faculty, staff, sponsors, and auditors. Able to interpret and communicate sponsor’s requirements. • Strong personal integrity, exhibits good judgment, attention to detail; critical thinking and strong analytical skills; proactive problem-solving abilities; able to manage task priorities and deadlines, and delegate tasks. Preferred Qualifications • Experience in sponsored projects in higher education. • Certified Research Administrator (CRA) or CFRA. • Sponsored projects-related audit experience • Demonstrated supervisory experience, including leading, training, and evaluating direct reports. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information $85,000-$95,000 Hours per week 40 hrs per week Review Date October 12, 2026 Additional Information The position is hybrid with a weekly on-campus presence and will require the completion of a telework agreement in accordance with Policy 4325, Alternative Work Site and Telework Policy. The hybrid work schedule will be confirmed following an onsite training period. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance .  These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Renee VanDyke at revandyke@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 3ec56d19 Last Name (required) 62b891e8 Email (required) c9bbb36b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 56ab1ef7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Grants / Contracts Business / Accounting / Finance Grants / Contracts Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Vice President for Research Vice President for Research First Name (required) 02d7c535 Last Name (required) 92f9260f Email (required) 096aa838 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) ad1677ff Last Name (required) a4bcb415 Email (required) e013bd51 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Academic Affairs Coordinator Blacksburg Virginia Dean - Architecture Join the College of Architecture, Arts, and Design's undergraduate academic affairs and advising team and contribute to the delivery of a positive student experience. Help us build a better future! Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Computer Science Blacksburg Virginia Computer Science Computer science is changing faster than ever, and today’s questions will shape the field for decades to come. Virginia Tech’s Department of Computer Science is seeking the next generation of faculty to help define what’s next. Apply today! Postdoctoral Associate Alexandria Virginia Housing Research Center Launch the next chapter of your research career with the Virginia Housing Research Center. As a Postdoctoral Associate, you'll work alongside leading researchers to explore housing innovation, inform policy decisions, and create positive impacts for communities throughout Virginia. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Get Directions See All Locations Contact Virginia Tech University Status Principles of Community Privacy Statement Acceptable Use We Remember University Libraries Accessibility Consumer Information Cost & Aid SAFE at VT Policies Equal Opportunity WVTF University Bookstore Jobs at Virginia Tech © 2026 Virginia Tech. All rights reserved. Facebook X Threads Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Please choose a senior management"
