    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/director-of-finance-and-business-operations-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Finance and Business Operations",
      "description": "Director of Finance and Business Operations - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Skip to main content Welcome Home About Virginia Tech Meet Our People Talk To Us Featured Departments Search Jobs My Profile Virginia Tech MENU Campus Photo Tour Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Get to Know Virginia Tech Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Network With Us Student Employment Virginia Tech Human Resources Applicant Login Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Director of Finance and Business Operations 537581 Blacksburg, Virginia IT Governance Planning and Strategy Administrative & Professional Vice President-Info Technology Add to favorites View favorites Job Description Virginia Tech is seeking an innovative and experienced leader to serve as Director of Finance and Business Operations for the Division of Information Technology. Reporting to the AVP for IT Governance, Planning, and Strategy, the director serves as the fiscal officer and leads the financial planning and business operations of the division. Financial Planning: The director provides counsel to the division’s senior leadership team through interpretation of actual financial data, development of in-year and future budget projections, and the analysis of actual financial activity and trends. The director reviews department organizational structures in terms of budget alignment and workflow and makes recommendations to align expenditures appropriately to track budgets at the department/initiative level. The director will be responsible for informing senior leadership about financial challenges, opportunities, and positioning within the university’s budget process. Business Operations: The director provides oversight of the Division of Information Technology’ auxiliary and self-supporting enterprises. The director establishes controls to ensure that all divisional financial obligations with vendors are met and that maintenance and software renewals are addressed. Leadership and Supervision: The director coaches, mentors and develops staff, clearly setting expectations for each position; recommends optimal organization and resource requirements to meet departmental goals; models and instills in all staff an exemplary customer service ethic and build cohesiveness as a team; develops training plans to meet new demands for the financial team; develops and maintains a positive and safe working environment in which open communication is fostered and employees demonstrate respect for each other. This role will support the redesign of existing processes, including budget and financial models, across the division and evaluate opportunities to improve service delivery models. This position requires a detailed-oriented professional with exceptional judgment and discretion, clear and concise communication skills, and deep analytical abilities. Required Qualifications • A master’s degree in business administration, finance, accounting, or related field, OR a bachelor's degree plus progressive experience that equates to a Master's degree. • Considerable knowledge of budgeting and planning in a nonprofit environment • Demonstrated ability to effectively organize, perform and supervise a large volume of varied management tasks • Detailed-oriented with exceptional judgment and discretion, clear and concise communication skills, and deep analytical abilities • Considerable experience in fund accounting and managing organizational expenditures within budget constraints Preferred Qualifications • Experience working with fiscal operations in a large university environment • Experience managing university auxiliary enterprises and self-supporting units • Experience working with Information Technology services Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information $180,000 - $198,000 Hours per week 40 Review Date 9/25/2026 Additional Information This position has a hybrid working arrangement with at least 3 days onsite in Blacksburg each week. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance .  These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact IT Human Resources at ithr@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 6909e85a Last Name (required) 7196b0ba Email (required) 4529d588 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 392eaf64 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Executive / Director / Management Business / Accounting / Finance Executive / Director / Management Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Vice President-Info Technology Vice President-Info Technology First Name (required) c819c979 Last Name (required) 83dec3f5 Email (required) bae63b4b Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have rea