    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/outreach-and-events-coordinator-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Outreach and Events Coordinator",
      "description": "Outreach and Events Coordinator - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Skip to main content Welcome Home About Virginia Tech Meet Our People Talk To Us Featured Departments Search Jobs My Profile Virginia Tech MENU Campus Photo Tour Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Get to Know Virginia Tech Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Network With Us Student Employment Virginia Tech Human Resources Applicant Login Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Outreach and Events Coordinator 537821 Blacksburg, Virginia Myers-Lawson School of Construction Administrative & Professional College of Engineering Add to favorites View favorites Job Description The Outreach and Events Coordinator serves as the primary point of contact for the planning, logistics, and execution of events and engagement activities serving students, faculty, alumni, industry partners, and other external constituents for the Myers-Lawson School of Construction (MLSoC). This position is responsible for planning and executing high-quality, strategically aligned events that advance the school’s outreach and engagement objectives, strengthen stakeholder connections, and enhance brand visibility. Reporting to the Associate Director of Outreach and Industry Engagement, this position is an integral member of the school's Outreach Team In addition to coordinating events, the Outreach and Events Coordinator manages the school's promotional inventory and branded merchandise in collaboration with the Outreach team and in accordance with MLSoC and VT brand standards. This position also provides logistical support for faculty-led site visits, field trips, and summer camps, and helps ensure the school offers a full slate of meaningful engagement opportunities that advance strategic goals and strengthen relationships with students, faculty, alumni, friends of the school, and industry. This role requires working occasionally in the evenings or on weekends in support of events. Required Qualifications • Master’s degree in marketing, communications, public relations, hospitality, event management, or related field or a bachelor’s degree with commiserate experience. • Experience managing events and/or working with alumni/external stakeholders. • Demonstrated experience coordinating venues, lodging, transportation, and catering logistics for multiple events annually. • Experience in higher education, advancement, or nonprofit event planning. Preferred Qualifications • Experience translating and aligning strategy into programs and events. • Demonstrated experience in developing post-event reports measuring attendance, engagement, satisfaction, and ROI. • Demonstrated ability to manage complex, high-visibility events. • Experience using CRM Systems (e.g. AIMS, Salesforce, etc.) Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information 55,000 - 60,000 Commensurate with experience Hours per week 40 hrs per week Review Date 10/12/2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance .  These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Sara Phillips at sara.phillips@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 8571272e Last Name (required) 4c17dfc7 Email (required) 181b64e7 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Ale