    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/science-technology-research-intelligence-analyst-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Science & Technology Research Intelligence Analyst",
      "description": "Science & Technology Research Intelligence Analyst - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Skip to main content Welcome Home About Virginia Tech Meet Our People Talk To Us Featured Departments Search Jobs My Profile Virginia Tech MENU Campus Photo Tour Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Get to Know Virginia Tech Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Network With Us Student Employment Virginia Tech Human Resources Applicant Login Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Science & Technology Research Intelligence Analyst 537820 Blacksburg, Virginia Library Administrative & Professional Dean of Libraries Add to favorites View favorites Job Description Reporting to the Director for Research Impact & Intelligence, the analyst will work in a team-based environment to provide consultations and deliver services related to documenting, collecting, and analyzing research and scholarly activity data to providing qualitative and quantitative evidence for strategic decision making through a variety of research domains. This analyst will also provide education and outreach on research intelligence, researcher visibility, finding funding opportunities, research analytics and tools, national research evaluation policy, and developing strategies for researchers and administrators to effectively Virginia Tech. The Science & Technology Research Intelligence Analyst will work with the team to provide specialized support for bibliometrics, network visualization options, and emerging applications of research ecosystem data. The incumbent will be liaison librarian to one program, department, or institute that is related to the incumbent’s background and/or expertise. The Science & Technology Research Intelligence Analyst will partner with colleagues across the Libraries and University (academic colleges, departments, institutes, and others Office of Research and Innovation, Institutional Effectiveness & Analytics, Office of the Provost), serve as liaison to Virginia Tech Transportation Institute, and support the Virginia Tech community across all locations, including distance and online affiliates, utilizing best practices to reflect Virginia Tech’s Principles of Community throughout work activities and initiatives. Required Qualifications -A terminal degree in a field related to the job duties, such as a master's in library and/or Information Science (MLS, MLIS, MIS, etc) from an ALA-accredited graduate program, or Ph.D or other terminal degree related to job duties. -Experience working as a professional in a large research-intensive university, national lab, or similar research-intensive institution -Education, training, or experience with one or more of the following: scholarly databases and their metadata, and/or related platforms, software, tools, or databases -Experience designing, planning, implementing, and maintaining complex projects or services -Evidence of knowledge, background, or experience in current and emerging trends or theories in academic research and scholarship Preferred Qualifications -An active research agenda demonstrated through published scholarly work -Experience with research, funding, and/or patent metrics, analysis methods, bibliographic databases, and research analytic software and/or tools such as Scival, InCites, or Academic Analytics -Experience providing services related to research, funding, and/or patent metrics, as well as experience in data management and/or data science -Experience in library services, institutional effectiveness, or intelligence work Working knowledge of Python or R Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information $68,000 minimum dependent on qualifications and experience Hours per week 40 Review Date 10/19/26 Additional Information Work Location: This position is eligible for hybrid or fully remote, and the work arrangement will be confirmed upon hire. As necessary, may need to be onsite for collaboration purposes, with up to four campus visits per year. Unable to Sponsor Work Visas. The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. The application package needs to include a resume, cover letter addressing the candidate’s experience with the responsibilities associated with the position, and the required and preferred qualifications, and the names of three(3) references and their contact information. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance .  These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Rebecca Osborne at rebeccaao@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) b3ce3d68 Last Name (required) 178f1c4f Email (required) 097ae9a2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 317e6b69 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Library Library Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management Dean of Libraries Dean of Libraries First Name (required) 295bab29 Last Name (required) 2fd8ac65 Email (required) b7390a2a Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 5271f770 Last Name (required) 3347aaa7 Email (required) 0cfa550b Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Academic Affairs Coordinator Blacksburg Virginia Dean - Architecture Join the College of Architecture, Arts, and Design's undergraduate academic affairs and advising team and contribute to the delivery of a positive student experience. Help us build a better future! Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Computer Science Blacksburg Virginia Computer Science Computer science is changing faster than ever, and today’s questions will shape the field for decades to come. Virginia Tech’s Department of Computer Science is seeking the next generation of faculty to help define what’s next. Apply today! Postdoctoral Associate Alexandria Virginia Housing Research Center Launch the next chapter of your research career with the Virginia Housing Research Center. As a Postdoctoral Associate, you'll work alongside leading researchers to explore housing innovation, inform policy decisions, and create positive impacts for communities throughout Virginia. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Get Directions See All Locations Contact Virginia Tech University Status Principles of Community Privacy Statement Acceptable Use We Remember University Libraries Accessibility Consumer Information Cost & Aid SAFE at VT Policies Equal Opportunity WVTF University Bookstore Jobs at Virginia Tech © 2026 Virginia Tech. All rights reserved. Facebook X Threads Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Please choose a senior management"
