    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/sr-associate-ad-business-operations-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Sr. Associate AD / Business Operations",
      "description": "Sr. Associate AD /  Business Operations - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Skip to main content Welcome Home About Virginia Tech Meet Our People Talk To Us Featured Departments Search Jobs My Profile Virginia Tech MENU Campus Photo Tour Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Get to Know Virginia Tech Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Network With Us Student Employment Virginia Tech Human Resources Applicant Login Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Sr. Associate AD /  Business Operations 537864 Blacksburg, Virginia Athletic Department Administrative & Professional President Add to favorites View favorites Job Description The Virginia Tech Department of Athletics embraces the core values of Integrity, Service, Honor, Excellence, and Strong Together. Guided by our motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), we are committed to fostering a culture that accepts, affirms, and values all individuals and their unique contributions to the department, university, and broader community. Reporting directly to the Executive Associate AD, Athletics CFO, the Sr. Assoc. AD / Business Operations will manage the day-to-day fiscal activities to include team/support budgeting, financial planning and analysis, procurement, financial reporting, affiliated organization support, and overall workflow management. This position will directly or indirectly oversee all business operations and business services positions. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in business/accounting or related field with significant experience, or a master's degree. Proven ability to build and implement strategic financial plans, including operating and capital, and to convey concepts to a broad audience including university senior level administrators. Strong interpersonal and communications skills. Proven leadership and supervisory skills. Well-developed ability to demonstrate technical expertise in financial planning, management, and analysis in order to provide senior leadership with highly developed decision support. Excellent organizational and analytical skills. Functional familiarity with standard desktop applications, with expertise required in Excel. Must be able to work effectively and willingly with diverse coworkers, students, and outside representatives. Preferred Qualifications Significant NCAA athletic financial management experience at the Division I level. First-hand familiarity with university fund accounting systems. Working knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations relevant to position. Pay Band {lPayScaleID} Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information Commensurate with experience. Hours per week 40+. Nights and weekends as needed. Review Date 10/6/2026 Additional Information See more about working in VT Athletics at https://hokiesports.com/be-a-hokie The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance .  These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Stuart Cochran at stuart@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 65bc78c6 Last Name (required) d68bae15 Email (required) 0b8c52e9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 086960e4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Business / Accounting / Finance Business / Accounting / Finance Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management President President First Name (required) f68c3546 Last Name (required) cc656ca8 Email (required) 30f786f8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Send Me This Job or Refer a Friend First Name (required) 7fcc19b0 Last Name (required) 3bc80c82 Email (required) a9bfff36 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Recommended Jobs For You Academic Affairs Coordinator Blacksburg Virginia Dean - Architecture Join the College of Architecture, Arts, and Design's undergraduate academic affairs and advising team and contribute to the delivery of a positive student experience. Help us build a better future! Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Computer Science Blacksburg Virginia Computer Science Computer science is changing faster than ever, and today’s questions will shape the field for decades to come. Virginia Tech’s Department of Computer Science is seeking the next generation of faculty to help define what’s next. Apply today! Postdoctoral Associate Alexandria Virginia Housing Research Center Launch the next chapter of your research career with the Virginia Housing Research Center. As a Postdoctoral Associate, you'll work alongside leading researchers to explore housing innovation, inform policy decisions, and create positive impacts for communities throughout Virginia. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Get Directions See All Locations Contact Virginia Tech University Status Principles of Community Privacy Statement Acceptable Use We Remember University Libraries Accessibility Consumer Information Cost & Aid SAFE at VT Policies Equal Opportunity WVTF University Bookstore Jobs at Virginia Tech © 2026 Virginia Tech. All rights reserved. Facebook X Threads Instagram LinkedIn YouTube Please choose a senior management"
