    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/tenure-track-faculty-position-in-computer-science-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Computer Science",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Computer Science - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Skip to main content Welcome Home About Virginia Tech Meet Our People Talk To Us Featured Departments Search Jobs My Profile Virginia Tech MENU Campus Photo Tour Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Get to Know Virginia Tech Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Network With Us Student Employment Virginia Tech Human Resources Applicant Login Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Tenure-Track Faculty Position in Computer Science 537614 Blacksburg, Virginia Computer Science Teaching & Research Faculty College of Engineering Add to favorites View favorites Job Description Tenure-Track Faculty in the Department of Computer Science hold full-time appointments with a workload allocation of approximately 40% teaching, 50% research, and 10% service. They are expected to develop nationally recognized research programs supported by external funding, disseminate their work in high-impact venues, and mentor both graduate and undergraduate students in research. Teaching responsibilities include undergraduate and graduate courses, curriculum development, and the use of effective and inclusive pedagogy. Tenure-Track Faculty also contribute to departmental, university, and professional service, consistent with Virginia Tech’s land-grant mission and commitment to Ut Prosim (“That I May Serve”). Their performance is evaluated annually, and advancement is governed by the university's promotion and tenure process. Required Qualifications - An earned doctoral degree in Computer Science or closely related field at the time of the appointment and a rank-appropriate record of scholarship and collaboration in computing research. - Record of significant research accomplishments (e.g. publications) and rank-appropriate record of professional service. - Ability to contribute to the department's teaching mission, at both graduate and undergraduate levels. Preferred Qualifications - Demonstrated interest in collaborative research in fields represented by department's existing faculty or planned hiring. - Demonstrated ability and willingness to work collaboratively with faculty from a variety of disciplines. - Recognition of research excellence as demonstrated by e.g. best paper or society awards. - Instructional experience in higher education. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Regular Salary Information $125,000-$135,000, annually Hours per week 40 Review Date 11/15/2026, open until filled Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance .  These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Joe Morgan at jmorgan99@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Back to job search Apply Now! First Name (required) 3af489f3 Last Name (required) 73c175a4 Email (required) 209080b1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Virginia Tech.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy and our SMS terms & conditions . Thank you! Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 9f1a5430 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Engineering Engineering Locations Blacksburg, Virginia Blacksburg, Virginia Senior Management College of Engineering College of Engineering First Name (required) 2509f9a7 Last Name (requir