    "https://jobs.apply.vt.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-student-success-programs-blacksburg-virginia-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Success Programs",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Student Success Programs - Blacksburg, Virginia, United States Skip to main content Welcome Home About Virginia Tech Meet Our People Talk To Us Featured Departments Search Jobs My Profile Virginia Tech MENU Campus Photo Tour Committed to Our Veterans and Military Dual Career Program Employment Process Frequently Asked Questions Get to Know Virginia Tech Moving and Relocation Resources Blacksburg and New River Valley Greater Washington, D.C., area Roanoke Network With Us Student Employment Virginia Tech Human Resources Applicant Login Kiosk mode Claim your role Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Director of Student Success Programs 537914 Blacksburg, Virginia Dean - Engineering Administrative & Professional College of Engineering Add to favorites View favorites Job Description The Assistant Director of Student Success Programs provides high-impact academic, professional, and personal support for undergraduate students within the College of Engineering from varied socioeconomic backgrounds. The Assistant Director will manage the day-to-day programmatic and operational needs of special programs, such as the Clark Scholars Program and Student Transition Engineering Program (STEP), ensuring each program runs smoothly and meets its goals within established guidelines and deadlines. The Assistant Director will help students connect to other student services to support retention, graduation, and individual well-being. In addition to leading these programs, the Assistant Director provides stewardship of meeting rooms and general-use spaces, ensuring these environments are well managed, welcoming, and supportive of student success and community building. This position reports to the Executive Director and requires a highly motivated individual who can deliver a high level of interactive customer service while developing and maintaining collaborative relationships within the College and University environment. Required Qualifications A Master’s degree (or a bachelor’s degree with relevant professional experience) in Engineering, Education, Counseling, Student Personnel Services, or a relevant field Experience working in a student-focused setting, such as academic advising, classroom instruction, counseling, or related student services. Demonstrated experience using Microsoft Office Suite or equivalent tools for document creation, data management, and electronic file organization in a professional setting. Ability to travel occasionally and work weekends as needed Preferred Qualifications Proven record of excellent interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills Demonstrated history of program or project management and event planning Experience hiring and supervising undergraduate students Experience owning a recurring newsletter or regular audience communication channel from concept to distribution. Overtime Status Exempt: Not eligible for overtime Appointment Type Restricted Salary Information $68,000 - $78,000 Commensurate with experience Hours per week 40 Review Date October 19, 2026 Additional Information The successful candidate will be required to have a criminal conviction check. About Virginia Tech Dedicated to its motto, Ut Prosim (That I May Serve), Virginia Tech pushes the boundaries of knowledge by taking a hands-on, transdisciplinary approach to preparing scholars to be leaders and problem-solvers. A comprehensive land-grant institution that enhances the quality of life in Virginia and throughout the world, Virginia Tech is an inclusive community dedicated to knowledge, discovery, and creativity. The university offers more than 280 majors to a diverse enrollment of more than 36,000 undergraduate, graduate, and professional students in eight undergraduate colleges , a school of medicine , a veterinary medicine college, Graduate School , and Honors College . The university has a significant presence across Virginia, including Blacksburg, the greater Washington, D.C. area, the Health Sciences and Technology Campus in Roanoke, sites in Newport News and Richmond, and numerous Extension offices and research institutes . A leading global research institution, Virginia Tech conducts more than $650 million in research annually. Virginia Tech endorses and encourages participation in professional development opportunities and university shared governance .  These valuable contributions to university shared governance provide important representation and perspective, along with opportunities for unique and impactful professional development. Virginia Tech does not discriminate against employees, students, or applicants on the basis of age, color, disability, sex (including pregnancy), gender, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, ethnicity or national origin, political affiliation, race, religion, sexual orientation, or military status, or otherwise discriminate against employees or applicants who inquire about, discuss, or disclose their compensation or the compensation of other employees or applicants, or on any other basis protected by law. If you are an individual with a disability and desire an accommodation, please contact Kayla Chaffin at chaffin@vt.edu during regular business hours at least 10 business days prior to the event. Recommended Jobs For You Patron Services Operations Manager Blacksburg Virginia Center for the Arts at VT Join the Center for the Arts at VT as our Patron Services Operations Manager and help shape the patron experience at the intersection of campus and community. This role blends leadership, operational oversight, and hands‑on house and rental management in a vibrant performing arts environment. Director of Marketing and Communications, College of Natural Resources and Environment Blacksburg Virginia Marketing and Communications The Director of Marketing and Communications for the College of Natural Resources and Environment (CNRE) is responsible for developing, planning, executing, and measuring a comprehensive, strategic marketing and communications program for the College of Natural Resources and Environment and aligning those activities with university-level communications, marketing, branding priorities, and initiatives. The marketing and communications program led by the Director will embody and reflect CNRE core values and principles, and the college’s unique attributes and offerings that contribute to the broader understanding of Virginia Tech. Agricultural  Specialist III Blackstone Virginia Southern Piedmont AREC Virginia Tech's Southern Piedmont Agricultural and Research and Extension Center (AREC) in Blackstone, Virginia, is accepting applications for an Agricultural Specialist III position to manage daily field, greenhouse and lab research. Candidate Details “This website uses cookies to improve your experience. We use cookies to personalize job recommendations, understand site traffic, and enhance your interaction with our career site. By clicking ‘I Accept’, you consent to our use of cookies. By clicking ‘I Do Not Accept’, only essential cookies will be used, but certain features may not function as intended. You can change your cookie settings at any time by clicking ‘Manage Cookies’. For more information, please review our Privacy Policy.” Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Cookies Performance Cookies Manage Cookies I do not accept I accept Save Get Directions See All Locations Contact Virginia Tech University Status Principles of Community Privacy Statement Acceptable Use We Remember University Libraries Accessibility Consumer Information Cost & Aid SAFE at VT Policies Equal Opportunity WVTF University Bookstore Jobs at Virginia Tech © 2026 Virginia Tech. All rights reserved. Facebook X Threads Instagram LinkedIn YouTube"
